      "summary": "A hands-on session about how each of us actually builds with AI day to day. Most of the time went to two themes: running models locally versus paying for cloud models, and showing real working setups. We compared local-model runners and hardware limits, walked through live project builds, and shared workflow tips for keeping AI projects organised and reasonably secure.\r\n\r\nThe recurring takeaway: local models are appealing (free, private) but need a strong GPU and still trail the paid cloud models on quality, so the practical answer is usually a mix, pick the cheapest tool that is good enough for the task.",
